{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"HARD ANODIZING"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 hole (D12) is a tight-tolerance fit feature, but the drawing calls for HARD ANODIZING in the title block without any allowance or note stating whether the H7 tolerance applies before or after anodizing. Hard anodize adds measurable thickness that will shrink the bore and can cause mating interference; the designer must specify if the dimension is pre- or post-coat and adjust limits accordingly."
    ,
    "recommended_correction":"Add a note clarifying that the H7 tolerance applies after hard anodizing (and adjust the machined size to allow for coating build-up), or state that the hole must be masked during anodizing."}]}
